// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row ptr_under_struct_field_region_escape_admitted (tier 1, `admits`).
// ILLEGAL PROGRAM ADMITTED: a raw pointer carried in a STRUCT FIELD launders the region
// it points through, and the reference obtained from it outlives the scope it borrowed.
//
//   struct Holder<'a> { q: *const &'a i64 }
//   fn first<'a>(h: Holder<'a>) -> &'a i64 { unsafe { *h.q } }
//
// `v` is dropped at the end of the inner block; `out` is read after it. logosc compiles
// this CLEAN (cc=0, no diagnostic) and the binary RUNS, exiting 7 — it reads the dead
// stack slot and happens to find the old value there. That is a use-after-scope the
// compiler never looked at.
//
// rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 MEASURED 2026-09-17: REFUSES,
//   error[E0597]: `v` does not live long enough
//   ... `v` dropped here while still borrowed / borrow later used here
// Twin: src/compiler/probes/2026-09-17b-ptrmentionland/rust/X05_ptr_in_struct_escapes_refuse.rs
//
// ⚠ IT IS THE CARRIER, NOT THE POINTER. The SAME escape written with the raw pointer as a
// BARE parameter (`fn raw<'a>(q: *mut &'a i64) -> &'a i64`) is REFUSED on this same binary,
// and so are the array and tuple carriers — all three by the `variance mismatch — expected
// *const &'static i64` sentence, i.e. refused by a DIFFERENT defect rather than by an
// escape check. The struct carrier reaches the callee binder by another route
// (`collect_param_regions_`'s Struct arm already inserts the field's region), so the
// accidental refusal never fires and nothing else catches it.
//
// FOUND 2026-09-17b-ptrmentionland as X05, a carrier variation written to price the
// abuse direction of a candidate arm. It reproduces on BASE with no probe installed:
// build_hash 8f5483d04b7c49ac 43. FIX = the program is REFUSED, with a diagnostic that
// names the escaping borrow (not the variance sentence).
package ptr_under_struct_field_region_escape_admitted;
struct Holder<'a> { q: *const &'a i64 }
fn first<'a>(h: Holder<'a>) -> &'a i64 {
    return unsafe { *h.q };
}
fn main() -> i32 {
    let out: &i64;
    {
        let v: i64 = 7i64;
        let r: &i64 = &v;
        let p: *const &i64 = &r;
        out = first(Holder { q: p });
    }
    return *out as i32;
}
